  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development introduces a highly vulnerable basement dwelling into Fluvial Flood Zone 2 which fails to pass the required Sequential and Exception Tests due to a restrictive site search methodology and an absence of exceptional wider sustainability benefits, whilst the submitted Flood Risk Assessment additionally fails to provide sufficient evidence regarding local groundwater levels or specific structural resilience measures to prevent water ingress, thereby failing to demonstrate that future occupants would not be placed at an unacceptable risk of flooding contrary to London Plan Policy SI 12, Kingston Core Strategy Policy DM4, and the National Planning Policy Framework",
    "The submitted Internal Daylight Assessment relies on a flawed methodology by assessing the combined kitchen and living area against an inappropriately low daylight target, which, compounded by the proposed windows falling significantly below the Vertical Sky Component guidelines due to severely restricted direct sky visibility, fails to demonstrate that adequate daylight and sunlight can be achieved within the constrained basement location, resulting in a poor standard of accommodation for future occupiers contrary to London Plan Policy D6, Kingston Core Strategy Policy DM10, the Residential Design SPD, and the National Planning Policy Framework."
  ],
